Avoid a division by zero in sctp_cwnd_update_after_packet_dropped().

A PKTDROP chunk reporting a bottleneck bandwidth/RTT that gives bw_avail == 0
and a current_onq smaller than the path MTU makes seg_onqueue = on_queue / mtu
zero, and my_portion = (incr * seg_inflight) / seg_onqueue divides by it
(SIGFPE natively, IntegerDivisionByZero trap on wasm). on_queue is raised to at
least flight_size first, so seg_onqueue == 0 implies seg_inflight == 0 and our
portion of the overage is 0.

Includes programs/test_pktdrop_cwnd.c: it plays the peer of a connecting socket
over AF_CONN and answers the INIT with a HEARTBEAT-ACK echoing a timestamp one
second old (the RTO then exceeds SCTP_SAT_NETWORK_MIN, so sat_network is set)
and a middle-box PKTDROP with bottle_bw 0 and current_onq 42. Without the fix
the test dies with SIGFPE.

Upstream: none found; related open PR sctplab/usrsctp#763 (issue #762) fixes a
division by zero in sctp_cwnd_update_after_fr().

